IMPORT prelude

-- Portuguese Missions Ordinance 1910 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "The Agent of the Commission for the Administration of the
-- Estates of the Portuguese Missions in China at Singapore" is and how a successor Agent becomes "duly qualified" (ss 2, 6), the
-- ten scheduled parcels vested in it and the 999-year terms they are held for (s 3 and the five Schedules), what it may do with
-- property (s 4), suing it and serving process on it (s 5), how its deeds are validly sealed and signed (s 7), and whose rights the
-- Ordinance leaves alone (s 8).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PMO1910.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". Two amendment
-- annotations appear in the body: "[Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]" under s 5 and "[7/97]" under s 8. The Ordinance is dated
-- 8 April 1910. The deposit's metadata records it as the current version as at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0241 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance (historical, private and spent Acts). It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no
-- scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The operative part is eight short sections, so the whole of it is in scope except the
-- short title. For a person outside the Commission it matters when buying, leasing or lending against the Corporation's land (ss 4,
-- 7), when suing it or serving it (s 5), and for title to the ten parcels in the Schedules (ss 3, 8).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the long recitals of the 1826-1865 leases, assignments and Portuguese Ordinances, except as they
-- explain the Schedules; the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, to which s 7(1) refers (whether a power
-- of attorney was "deposited" under it is a stated fact); the boundaries of each parcel; whether any parcel is still held (the deposit
-- does not say); the Commission's internal governance.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Portuguese Missions Ordinance 1910 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2 and 6 -- who is the Corporation, and when a successor Agent is duly qualified`

-- s 2(1): "Antonio Augusto Cardozo, Agent at Singapore, and his successors for the time being in the office of Agent ... duly qualified
-- as hereinafter provided, shall be a body corporate, hereinafter called the Corporation", with perpetual succession and a seal.
-- s 6(1): "No person other than the said Antonio Augusto Cardozo shall be deemed to be duly qualified as aforesaid unless and until he
-- has been duly appointed ... by the Bishop of Macao, as President of the aforesaid Commission, by instrument in writing, and such
-- instrument has been produced to the Minister and the same approved by him and unless and until a notification of such approval has
-- appeared in the Gazette."
-- s 6(2): "Such notification shall be sufficient evidence of the appointment and that the person named therein is duly qualified".
--
-- Four steps, all required, and the last is the Gazette: a successor appointed and approved but not yet gazetted is not yet the
-- Corporation. Cardozo, named in 1910, needed none of them. The notification is "sufficient", not "conclusive", evidence.
DECLARE Agent HAS
    `is Antonio Augusto Cardozo` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is appointed by the Bishop of Macao as President by instrument in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the instrument was produced to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister approved it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the approval was notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the agent` IS AN Agent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is duly qualified` IF
        `the agent`'s `is Antonio Augusto Cardozo`
    OR  (    `the agent`'s `is appointed by the Bishop of Macao as President by instrument in writing`
         AND `the agent`'s `the instrument was produced to the Minister`
         AND `the agent`'s `the Minister approved it`
         AND `the agent`'s `the approval was notified in the Gazette`)

GIVEN `the agent` IS AN Agent
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Gazette is sufficient evidence of qualification` IF
    `the agent`'s `the approval was notified in the Gazette`

§§ `3 and the Schedules -- the ten parcels and their terms`

-- s 3: "Subject to section 8, all the properties comprised in the Schedules are hereby vested in the Corporation for the residue of
-- the term of years under which the same are held for the use and behoof of the Portuguese Missions in China."
-- Each Schedule item is a piece of land in Singapore Town demised by lease "for the term of 999 years". Items are numbered 1-10 across
-- the five Schedules. Items 1-8 run from the date of their own lease. Item 9 (lease Lot No. 2 of lease No. 1577, dated 3 March 1865)
-- runs "from the day of the date of the original lease No. 1577 dated 5 November 1862". Item 10 (lease No. 300, dated 7 May 1841)
-- runs "from the 11 June 1827". Rents and areas are as the Schedules state them, in dollars and square metres.
DECLARE Parcel IS ONE OF
    `item 1, High Street, lease 205`
    `item 2, High Street, lease 555`
    `item 3, lease 1 of Grant 554`
    `item 4, North Bridge Road to Beach Road, lease 208`
    `item 5, Commercial Square, lease 34`
    `item 6, Commercial Square, lease 35`
    `item 7, Commercial Square, lease 36`
    `item 8, Commercial Square to the Sea, lease 12`
    `item 9, Lot 2 of lease 1577`
    `item 10, New Bridge Road and the Singapore River, lease 300`

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule it is in` `the parcel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `item 1, High Street, lease 205` THEN 1
    WHEN `item 2, High Street, lease 555` THEN 1
    WHEN `item 3, lease 1 of Grant 554` THEN 1
    WHEN `item 4, North Bridge Road to Beach Road, lease 208` THEN 2
    WHEN `item 5, Commercial Square, lease 34` THEN 3
    WHEN `item 6, Commercial Square, lease 35` THEN 3
    WHEN `item 7, Commercial Square, lease 36` THEN 3
    WHEN `item 8, Commercial Square to the Sea, lease 12` THEN 4
    WHEN `item 9, Lot 2 of lease 1577` THEN 4
    WHEN `item 10, New Bridge Road and the Singapore River, lease 300` THEN 5

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the annual rent in dollars` `the parcel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `item 1, High Street, lease 205` THEN 20
    WHEN `item 2, High Street, lease 555` THEN 27
    WHEN `item 3, lease 1 of Grant 554` THEN 15.50
    WHEN `item 4, North Bridge Road to Beach Road, lease 208` THEN 30
    WHEN `item 5, Commercial Square, lease 34` THEN 14.50
    WHEN `item 6, Commercial Square, lease 35` THEN 14.50
    WHEN `item 7, Commercial Square, lease 36` THEN 14.50
    WHEN `item 8, Commercial Square to the Sea, lease 12` THEN 80
    WHEN `item 9, Lot 2 of lease 1577` THEN 28
    WHEN `item 10, New Bridge Road and the Singapore River, lease 300` THEN 28.37

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the area in square metres` `the parcel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `item 1, High Street, lease 205` THEN 3036.1
    WHEN `item 2, High Street, lease 555` THEN 2428.1
    WHEN `item 3, lease 1 of Grant 554` THEN 1412.5
    WHEN `item 4, North Bridge Road to Beach Road, lease 208` THEN 8039.6
    WHEN `item 5, Commercial Square, lease 34` THEN 700.3
    WHEN `item 6, Commercial Square, lease 35` THEN 696.8
    WHEN `item 7, Commercial Square, lease 36` THEN 696.8
    WHEN `item 8, Commercial Square to the Sea, lease 12` THEN 2739.5
    WHEN `item 9, Lot 2 of lease 1577` THEN 955.8
    WHEN `item 10, New Bridge Road and the Singapore River, lease 300` THEN 4476.8

-- The year the lease instrument is dated.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of the lease instrument` `the parcel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `item 1, High Street, lease 205` THEN 1827
    WHEN `item 2, High Street, lease 555` THEN 1828
    WHEN `item 3, lease 1 of Grant 554` THEN 1831
    WHEN `item 4, North Bridge Road to Beach Road, lease 208` THEN 1827
    WHEN `item 5, Commercial Square, lease 34` THEN 1826
    WHEN `item 6, Commercial Square, lease 35` THEN 1826
    WHEN `item 7, Commercial Square, lease 36` THEN 1826
    WHEN `item 8, Commercial Square to the Sea, lease 12` THEN 1826
    WHEN `item 9, Lot 2 of lease 1577` THEN 1865
    WHEN `item 10, New Bridge Road and the Singapore River, lease 300` THEN 1841

-- The year the 999-year term runs from. Differs from the instrument's year for items 9 and 10 only.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year the term runs from` `the parcel` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the parcel`
    WHEN `item 9, Lot 2 of lease 1577` THEN 1862
    WHEN `item 10, New Bridge Road and the Singapore River, lease 300` THEN 1827
    OTHERWISE `the year of the lease instrument` `the parcel`

GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term runs from a date other than the lease's own date` IF
    NOT `the year the term runs from` `the parcel` EQUALS `the year of the lease instrument` `the parcel`

-- The anniversary year in which the 999-year term ends. Year arithmetic only; the day and month are those of the start date.
GIVEN `the parcel` IS A Parcel
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year the term ends` `the parcel` MEANS
    `the year the term runs from` `the parcel` PLUS 999

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total annual rent of the scheduled parcels` MEANS
          `the annual rent in dollars` `item 1, High Street, lease 205`
    PLUS  `the annual rent in dollars` `item 2, High Street, lease 555`
    PLUS  `the annual rent in dollars` `item 3, lease 1 of Grant 554`
    PLUS  `the annual rent in dollars` `item 4, North Bridge Road to Beach Road, lease 208`
    PLUS  `the annual rent in dollars` `item 5, Commercial Square, lease 34`
    PLUS  `the annual rent in dollars` `item 6, Commercial Square, lease 35`
    PLUS  `the annual rent in dollars` `item 7, Commercial Square, lease 36`
    PLUS  `the annual rent in dollars` `item 8, Commercial Square to the Sea, lease 12`
    PLUS  `the annual rent in dollars` `item 9, Lot 2 of lease 1577`
    PLUS  `the annual rent in dollars` `item 10, New Bridge Road and the Singapore River, lease 300`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total area of the scheduled parcels` MEANS
          `the area in square metres` `item 1, High Street, lease 205`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 2, High Street, lease 555`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 3, lease 1 of Grant 554`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 4, North Bridge Road to Beach Road, lease 208`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 5, Commercial Square, lease 34`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 6, Commercial Square, lease 35`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 7, Commercial Square, lease 36`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 8, Commercial Square to the Sea, lease 12`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 9, Lot 2 of lease 1577`
    PLUS  `the area in square metres` `item 10, New Bridge Road and the Singapore River, lease 300`

-- s 3 vests only property "comprised in the Schedules", and only for "the residue of the term of years". Other property the
-- Corporation holds comes to it under s 4, not s 3.
GIVEN `is comprised in a Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN, `the term of years has run out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 vests it in the Corporation` IF
    `is comprised in a Schedule` AND (NOT `the term of years has run out`)

§§ `4 -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do with property`

-- s 4: "The Corporation may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description within the
-- Colony, and sell, convey, assign, exchange, surrender, yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer or otherwise howsoever dispose
-- of or deal with any movable or immovable property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as to the Corporation seem fit."
--
-- Acquiring is limited to property "within the Colony"; disposing is limited to property "vested in the Corporation". The disposal
-- limb carries no "within the Colony" words (encoded as written). The Ordinance confers no power to borrow without security.
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `acquire or purchase property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell property`
    `exchange property`
    `mortgage property`
    `lease property`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is within the Colony` IS A BOOLEAN, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `acquire or purchase property` THEN `the property is within the Colony`
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN `the property is within the Colony`
    WHEN `sell property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `exchange property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `lease property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5 -- suing the Corporation and serving it`

-- s 5(1): "The Corporation may sue and be sued and take all legal proceedings in any of the Courts of the Colony" by its corporate name.
-- s 5(2): "All originating claims, notices and legal process may be served upon the Corporation by being left at the residence for
-- the time being in Singapore of the Corporation." [Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]
--
-- Unlike the Bishop of Singapore Ordinance, the capacity to sue and be sued is not confined to the Corporation's property. s 5(2) says
-- "may": it authorises one mode of service without saying it is the only one. Whether another mode is good depends on law outside this
-- text and is not encoded; the rule below answers only whether s 5(2) itself authorises the mode.
DECLARE ServiceMode IS ONE OF
    `left at the Corporation's residence in Singapore`
    `left at one of the scheduled parcels that is not the residence`
    `sent to the Bishop of Macao`

GIVEN `the mode` IS A ServiceMode
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5(2) authorises the service` IF
    CONSIDER `the mode`
    WHEN `left at the Corporation's residence in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 7(1): no instrument sealed with the Corporation's seal "shall be deemed to be duly sealed unless such seal has been affixed in the
-- presence of the said Antonio Augusto Cardozo or his attorney duly authorised by a power of attorney deposited under section 48 of
-- the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, or in the presence of his successor ... duly qualified as aforesaid, or his attorney
-- duly authorised as aforesaid, and unless such deed, document or other instrument is signed by" one of the same.
-- s 7(2): "Such signing shall be taken as sufficient evidence of the due sealing of such deed or document or other instrument."
--
-- A successor who is not yet "duly qualified" under s 6 (for example, not yet gazetted) cannot validly witness the seal or sign, and
-- neither can his attorney. Witness and signer need not be the same person on the words of s 7(1); that reading is encoded.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `Antonio Augusto Cardozo`
    `Cardozo's attorney under a deposited power`
    `a duly qualified successor Agent`
    `a qualified successor's attorney under a deposited power`
    `a successor Agent not yet gazetted`
    `an attorney whose power is not deposited`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may witness the seal and sign` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `Antonio Augusto Cardozo` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Cardozo's attorney under a deposited power` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a duly qualified successor Agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a qualified successor's attorney under a deposited power` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is duly sealed under section 7` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may witness the seal and sign` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`)
    AND `may witness the seal and sign` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence of due sealing` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `may witness the seal and sign` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

§§ `8 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 8: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the rights of the Government, or any bodies politic or corporate or of any other
-- persons, except such as are mentioned in this Ordinance, and those claiming by, from and under them or any of the legal personal
-- representatives of the said Isaiah Zechariah, Joaquim Jozé Leite, Liete or Letta, Nicholao Rodrigues Pereira de Borja or Manuel
-- Lourenço de Gouvêa or any persons claiming by, through, from, or under them."
--
-- Read here (an inference from the sentence, whose punctuation allows other readings) as: the Ordinance may affect the rights only of
-- persons mentioned in it, those claiming under them, and the legal personal representatives of the four named men and those claiming
-- under the representatives. Everyone else's rights, the Government's included, are untouched -- and s 3 is "Subject to section 8".
GIVEN `is mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN, `is or claims under a legal personal representative of one of the four named men` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
        `is mentioned in the Ordinance`
    OR  `claims by, from or under a person mentioned`
    OR  `is or claims under a legal personal representative of one of the four named men`
